% --- 19th-century historical roots (AVE's two lineages) ---
% Root 1 — the formulation (Maxwell quaternion EM -> Heaviside-Gibbs vector calculus).
% Root 2 — the ontology (Kelvin vortex-knot atom, on Helmholtz's vortex theorems; Tait's knot tables).
% The two most historian-contested claims (Maxwell-quaternion; Heaviside's reformulation)
% verified 2026-06-17 against secondary sources, NOT the corpus inline "Fact" tag:
%   - Maxwell's Treatise (1873) listed the EM equations in quaternion (Hamilton S./V.) form
%     at chapter ends, though not written exclusively in quaternions (History of Maxwell's
%     equations: "all the equations are listed and set in quaternion form").
%   - The vector-calculus reformulation was Heaviside (1884), concurrently with Gibbs and
%     Hertz; Gibbs's vector analysis was published as Wilson's Vector Analysis (1901).

