% --- Deletion 3 — the frame (the relativity lineage: FitzGerald/Lorentz -> Poincare -> Einstein) ---
% The constructive route (FitzGerald 1889, Lorentz 1892/1904) derived the relativistic
% transformations FROM a medium; Einstein's 1905 principle theory recast them with no medium.
% Each canonical citation verified 2026-06-17 against secondary sources (WebFetch), not an
% inline corpus "Fact" tag:
%   - FitzGerald (1889): the contraction note, Science 13(328):390 ("The Ether and the
%     Earth's Atmosphere").
%   - Lorentz (1892): independent contraction ("De relatieve beweging van de aarde en den
%     aether"), Versl. Kon. Akad. Wet. Amsterdam 1:74-79.
%   - Lorentz (1904): the transformation ("Electromagnetic phenomena ..."), Proc. R. Neth.
%     Acad. Arts Sci. 6:809-831.
%   - Poincare (1905): the short Comptes Rendus note "Sur la dynamique de l'electron",
%     C. R. Acad. Sci. 140:1504-1508; (1906): the long Palermo paper, Rend. Circ. Mat.
%     Palermo 21:129-176 (received 1905, published Jan 1906).
